specs/hal-engine-commit-open-entries/spec.md:33:- Text the thinking-tag parser still held back, a tail that might have opened a tag, is flushed into the entry before it is flagged, so a cut-off answer keeps everything the model produced, as a `stop` already did ([validated by: keeps the text the thinking-tag parser still held when a throw cuts the answer short](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L659)).
